1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,282
The argument ended yesterday, you have already

2
00:00:03,282 --> 00:00:06,492
made peace, yet you still feel trapped in it.

3
00:00:06,492 --> 00:00:09,892
This is the second of three videos in which I

4
00:00:09,892 --> 00:00:11,932
explain anxious attachment.

5
00:00:11,932 --> 00:00:14,156
And this is the most confusing sign:

6
00:00:14,156 --> 00:00:17,492
everything is resolved outside, but what about inside?

7
00:00:17,492 --> 00:00:20,117
When the discussion ends, the other person

8
00:00:20,117 --> 00:00:23,492
goes back to normal, but you keep replaying the scene,

9
00:00:23,492 --> 00:00:26,461
looking for what you said wrong and checking

10
00:00:26,461 --> 00:00:29,092
the tone of the last message they sent.

11
00:00:29,092 --> 00:00:31,686
It is not resentment. It is your nervous

12
00:00:31,686 --> 00:00:35,252
system checking whether the bond and the love survived.

13
00:00:35,252 --> 00:00:38,712
Very often there is a child in the past who

14
00:00:38,712 --> 00:00:42,252
learned that after an argument or a mistake,

15
00:00:42,252 --> 00:00:44,919
someone disappeared. It could be days of

16
00:00:44,919 --> 00:00:48,052
silence or affection that returned differently.

17
00:00:48,052 --> 00:00:51,132
She learned not to relax until proof arrived

18
00:00:51,132 --> 00:00:53,652
that everything was all right again.

19
00:00:53,732 --> 00:00:56,949
But proof is never enough, because fear does

20
00:00:56,949 --> 00:01:00,532
not ask for proof. It asks for presence and care.

21
00:01:00,532 --> 00:01:03,382
What changes this is not controlling yourself

22
00:01:03,382 --> 00:01:06,169
more. It is your body learning that conflict

23
00:01:06,169 --> 00:01:07,372
is not abandonment,

24
00:01:07,372 --> 00:01:10,086
and your nervous system learning to relax.

25
00:01:10,086 --> 00:01:13,252
Tomorrow is the third video, and the hardest one,

26
00:01:13,252 --> 00:01:16,474
because you only calm down when the person

27
00:01:16,474 --> 00:01:18,852
replies. If this describes you,

28
00:01:18,852 --> 00:01:21,828
send it to someone who also spends days inside

29
00:01:21,828 --> 00:01:23,252
a ten-minute argument.

